					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-5333129#post-3720963</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-5333129/scp-150#post-3720963</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sat, 24 Feb 2018 17:07:55 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Decibelles</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2005044</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <blockquote> <p>SCP-150 reproduces during this assimilation process: as the lungs are assimilated, more eggs are produced and spread by the patient's coughing. Although as many as 10,000 eggs may be produced during this time, it is estimated that only 1% of them find their way into another host, of which 1% survive the host's immune response and implant successfully.</p> </blockquote> <p>It's very hard to effectively track it, not to mention it's hard to tell who is infected because of how the parasite works. I imagine in-universe, there'd be a lot more explicit details about how to track it and where to locate it.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
